      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about that too, but `report_ap_reset()` doesn\u0027t actually mean \"report to everyone\", just \"report to reset log\". So, it felt like overloading the function with unrelated work:\n\n`include/chipset.h`\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_CMD_AP_RESET_LOG\n\n/**\n * Report that the AP is being reset to the reset log.\n */\nvoid report_ap_reset(enum chipset_shutdown_reason reason);\n\n#else\n\nstatic inline void report_ap_reset(enum chipset_shutdown_reason reason)\n{\n}\n\n#endif /* !CONFIG_CMD_AP_RESET_LOG */\n```\n\nAlso, since `hook_notify(HOOK_CHIPSET_RESET)` is currently being called manually, we\u0027d need to make sure no one is calling it twice: both explicitly in whatever chipset reset function and implicitly by `report_ap_reset()`. We could check that somewhat with unit testing on zephyr boards, but I\u0027m not sure about the non-Zephyr boards, so that change is a bit more risky.\n\nAll that being said, I agree that this is the type of thing that should  be a lot more automatic for all boards/chipsets. It\u0027s surprising to see that we\u0027ve been missing this notification all along.",
      "parentUuid": "f1553021_a055cb6e",
